   {
    "id": "L1",
    "type": "mc",
    "text": "Find $lim[x->1] frac{x^2 - 1}{x - 1}$. Plugging in gives $frac{0}{0}$. Both are 0 at $x = 1$, so both have a factor of",
    "options": [
     "$(x - 1)$",
     "$(x + 1)$",
     "$x$",
     "$(x^2 - 1)$"
    ],
    "answer": 0,
    "hint": "A polynomial that is 0 at $x = 1$ has $(x - 1)$ as a factor.",
    "explain": "That shared factor is what makes $frac{0}{0}$."
   },
   {
    "id": "L2",
    "type": "steps",
    "text": "Finish $lim[x->1] frac{x^2 - 1}{x - 1}$.",
    "steps": [
